# Topic: buffer.readvectorf32x2/x3 and buffer.writevectorf32x2/x3
#
# What it does: adds the four buffer functions Roblox release 747 announces (two or three contiguous little-endian
# binary32 values read into, or written from, a vector's first components; a read zeroes the rest), as library
# functions with fastcall builtins (four LBF ids after LBF_TABLE_CLEAR) and the profiler's shapes for them. They check
# their arguments in the order and with the messages of buffer.readf32 / buffer.writef32. Native code calls the
# builtins; it has no inline lowering of its own.
#
# Why upstream lacks it: Roblox wrote its implementation internally (luau-lang/rfcs pull 198 is the design) and no
# release up to 0.746 carries it. This one follows the RFC and Roblox's documentation, not Roblox's code: when a
# release brings the functions, drop this topic in the bump (it conflicts with theirs in every table it touches) and
# move the profiler's shapes to upstream's builtin ids.

